# Everything here is excluded from the build context, which means it can never
# end up inside an image layer. An image layer is an artifact: it gets pushed to
# a registry, cached on build machines and pulled by anything that can deploy —
# so a secret baked into a layer is a secret leaked to every one of those places,
# permanently, even if a later layer "deletes" it.

# --- version control & CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- secrets & key material -------------------------------------------------
# The critical additions. `runtime/` holds the generated OTP pepper and the
# SQLite database (real student records); `.env` holds every credential. Neither
# belongs in an image — both are supplied at *run* time via the environment and a
# mounted volume.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
runtime/
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
.otp_pepper
*.secret

# --- local databases & dumps ------------------------------------------------
data/*.db
data/*.db-*
data/events.jsonl
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Python & tooling caches ------------------------------------------------
.venv
.venv-win
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- build artifacts & docs that the runtime does not need -------------------
dist
build
out
node_modules
docs
*.md
!README.md

# --- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
